    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d58">

                <pb facs="0160" n="54" sameAs="frus:frus1933-39/pg54"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.51W89 U.S.S.R./19: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in France</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Marriner</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Acting Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1933-12-27T11:00:00+00:00">December 27,
                            1933—11 a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 1:20 p.m.<anchor n="50" xml:id="d58-f1"/>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>578. For the Acting Secretary and Assistant Secretary Moore only from Bullitt.
                    Soviet Commercial Attaché, Paris, handed me last night list obligations in
                    reichsmarks of the S.S.S.R.<anchor n="51" xml:id="d58-f2"/> falling due in the
                    year <pb facs="0161" n="55" xml:id="pg55"/> 1934. He did not give me list of
                    obligations in dollars falling due in Germany for the same period but promised
                    to telegraph to Berlin at once for it. To cable this list in confidential code
                    is impossible without breaking the code since the Soviet Government has the list
                    and Marriner and I have agreed that the best method of
                    transmission is the following:</p>
                <p>[Here follows instruction as to method of transmitting the information to the
                        Department.<anchor n="52" xml:id="d58-f3"/>]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <list>
                            <item>[Bullitt]</item>
                            <item>
                                
                                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Marriner</hi>
                                
                            </item>
                        </list>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d58-f1" n="50" xml:id="d58-f1-content">
                <p>Telegram in two sections.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d58-f2" n="51" xml:id="d58-f2-content">
                <p>Soyuz SotsiaUsticheskikh Sovietskikh Respublik.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d58-f3" n="52" xml:id="d58-f3-content">
                <p>The information was duly sent in telegram No. 579, December 28, 11 a.m.
                    (800.51W89 U.S.S.R./20).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
